1
00:00:13,805 --> 00:00:17,726
Weather Forecast!

2
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,813
When did you take it from me?

3
00:00:21,896 --> 00:00:24,441
Was it when Jolyne blasted you?

4
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:25,942
Give it back immediately.

5
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:27,819
It belongs to me.

6
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:30,864
You don't understand what you're doing.

7
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:33,575
He's starting to remember.

8
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:35,326
Look, he's here.

9
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:41,958
Rainbows. There are rainbows!
The devil's rainbows!

10
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:43,710
It's Heavy Forecast!

11
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:49,382
Weather, what's the matter?

12
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,009
What are you doing?

13
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:58,016
What's your problem, punk?

14
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:00,852
I was sitting here first.

15
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:04,522
Don't touch me, I'll kill you!

16
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,782
Hey! You can't take
an injured person's seat--

17
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,494
Stop fussing.

18
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:20,455
You want him to sit, do you?

19
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:26,336
He can sit on you then.

20
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:31,257
Weather! What are you doing?

21
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:32,675
He's not an enemy!

22
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,719
He's just a nurse!

23
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:41,810
Now, sit all you want, crutch guy.

24
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:45,021
I've never felt better.

25
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:49,317
Wait up!

26
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,319
Weather, where do you think you're going?

27
00:01:52,612 --> 00:01:55,490
Weather? Don't Weather me.

28
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:57,784
So I go by Weather Forecast now.

29
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:02,247
Not a bad name.

30
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,960
What happened to him?

31
00:02:07,043 --> 00:02:08,211
It's as if…

32
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:10,713
he's gained an entirely new personality!

33
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:47,810
EPISODE 30: HEAVY FORECAST (1)

34
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:49,062
Rainbows!

35
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:52,565
Rainbows are closing in on us!

36
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:58,154
Jolyne, we have no time to waste!

37
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,322
This looks serious!

38
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:01,658
It's over!

39
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:03,493
Meet your end!

40
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:12,961
- What the hell?
- Ermes?

41
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,923
What just happened?

42
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:19,676
- Was it an illusion?
- This is bad.

43
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:23,137
Your life is in danger, but so is mine.

44
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:25,306
You untied yourself.

45
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:27,558
I'm warning you.

46
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:29,894
Don't touch those rainbows.

47
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:34,107
Those are Weather Forecast's rainbows
Father Pucchi sealed up!

48
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:37,652
Weather Forecast's Stand ability
controls the weather.

49
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,822
Do you understand what this means?

50
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:45,910
With his memory restored,
he can even destroy the ozone layer.

51
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:49,580
The ozone is even higher than the sky.

52
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:52,500
What could come
from messing with the ozone?

53
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,670
I can only say that it won't end well,

54
00:04:55,753 --> 00:04:57,380
but we're all in danger.

55
00:04:57,463 --> 00:04:59,841
The survival of humanity is at stake!

56
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:01,843
It was a risky sacrifice,

57
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:05,763
but I used Weather Forecast
to save my skin!

58
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:09,726
What did the ozone do to my Smack?

59
00:05:09,809 --> 00:05:14,397
Answer me. Do these rainbows mean
that Weather's memory is back?

60
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:17,066
The rainbows come out
from his subconscious.

61
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:22,405
Weather Forecast's Stand
has an automatic attack.

62
00:05:22,488 --> 00:05:25,116
The weather is a complex phenomenon.

63
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:28,786
His ability manifests in ways
he doesn't realize.

64
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:34,125
His memory should never
have been returned to him.

65
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:35,209
I'll tell you this.

66
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:38,629
To stop the rainbows,
you must kill Weather,

67
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:41,841
or extract his memory again.

68
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:46,637
Jolyne, can you kill Weather?

69
00:05:46,721 --> 00:05:50,600
If not, then humanity may end
before the new moon.

70
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:56,105
Though, I won't end here.

71
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:01,486
You shouldn't let Versus escape.

72
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:06,074
Versus fled, Jolyne!

73
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:11,412
There are two women here!

74
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:13,498
- Officer!
- Officer!

75
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:15,041
This is…

76
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,542
Was the hole this shallow?

77
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:19,754
He deactivated Netherworld and took off!

78
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:24,717
Where did they go?

79
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,427
Did you see two men running off?

80
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:27,595
Which way did they go?

81
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:29,347
Before we get to that,

82
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,015
I've seen your faces…

83
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,809
On a wanted fugitives list!

84
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,437
Rainbows. Just what is going on?

85
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:38,523
It's everywhere!

86
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,524
Hey!

87
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:44,153
What's going on?

88
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:45,404
You two!

89
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:47,406
You're the escaped convicts!

90
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:59,043
Don't go anywhere!

91
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:02,088
Get over here!

92
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:07,218
- Don't touch the rainbows!
- Stay away from them!

93
00:07:08,302 --> 00:07:09,720
Jolyne!

94
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:21,482
What do we do?

95
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:24,902
This is terrible!

96
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:30,158
What is going on?

97
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:33,077
Anyone who touches a rainbow
secretes snails!

98
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:37,498
I've seen Weather rain down
frogs in a storm.

99
00:07:38,082 --> 00:07:40,835
But these snails are entirely different.

100
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:43,212
How does this phenomenon relate
to Weather Forecast

101
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:45,798
and his ability to manipulate the weather?

102
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:47,133
Not only that,

103
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:52,513
once infected by the snails,
people are losing their minds. 

104
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:55,057
You can't run!

105
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:07,403
What is going on?

106
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:08,404
Ermes!

107
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:13,618
Jolyne! Are you okay?

108
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:15,286
Yeah.

109
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:17,622
Ermes.

110
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:20,625
Compared to normal people,
Stand Users may have a tolerance

111
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:22,960
to this kind of phenomenon.

112
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,962
So Jolyne,

113
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:27,048
who should we target?

114
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:29,467
Who do we need to defeat?

115
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:31,469
Is Weather Forecast an enemy,

116
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:35,264
or do we keep going after the priest?

117
00:08:35,348 --> 00:08:37,558
Tell me, who do we get rid of?

118
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:44,815
Weather Forecast, with his memories,
is our enemy!

119
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:47,944
No! Weather Forecast is our ally.

120
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,654
He's not our enemy!

121
00:08:49,737 --> 00:08:51,280
We have to find Versus.

122
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:53,074
Just like the priest said,

123
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:55,159
we can't let Versus go free.

124
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:58,496
His ability is to excavate memories.

125
00:08:58,579 --> 00:09:01,082
Maybe we can unearth
Weather's memory disc,

126
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:03,584
and stop this bizarre phenomenon.

127
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:05,044
I like your line of thinking.

128
00:09:05,127 --> 00:09:06,379
But first,

129
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:09,215
we need to get out of this hospital!

130
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:22,353
Hey! Where are you headed, Weather?

131
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:25,022
Is that where Jolyne is?

132
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:26,482
Tell me!

133
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:28,568
Shit.

134
00:09:31,529 --> 00:09:33,072
I want it.

135
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:35,741
I want that power.

136
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:38,035
I need to get it before the priest!

137
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:39,996
The power to attain heaven.

138
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:42,582
I want to live a good life!

139
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:46,502
What should be my next course of action?

140
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,671
Netherworld!

141
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,548
Found it.

142
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:54,594
The memory of the ground
when these two arrived at the hospital.

143
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:55,678
Ermes.

144
00:09:56,262 --> 00:10:00,182
Now is our chance,
when we go after Father Pucchi.

145
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,183
So don't worry.

146
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,101
What?

147
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:05,605
My father's disc can be sent
to the Speedwagon Foundation,

148
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:09,317
while we have Father Pucchi's attention.

149
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,569
Emporio will not fail.

150
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:14,238
Father will finally come back to us.

151
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:19,785
So Emporio is the ally's name
whom Jolyne was calling.

152
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:21,454
I have to find him.

153
00:10:22,038 --> 00:10:24,749
It's someone
even the priest wasn't aware of.

154
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,627
I don't know what Emporio looks like,

155
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:29,420
since I haven't dug up a memory of him.

156
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:31,172
But with all this commotion going on,

157
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:34,967
Jotaro Kujo's disc must still be with him.

158
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:37,261
He hasn't gotten it to this foundation.

159
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:41,974
Jotaro's disc gave the priest
the idea of getting into heaven.

160
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:44,852
If I get a hold of that disc,

161
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:46,729
even I can go to heaven!

162
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:48,939
The rainbows are my chance!

163
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:52,943
Jotaro's disc belongs to me!

164
00:10:55,071 --> 00:10:59,241
These snails are multiplying so fast,
they've covered the entire floor!

165
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:02,745
They won't stop reproducing!

166
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:05,539
Snails are asexual.

167
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:08,501
They pierce each other with love darts.

168
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:11,253
Both snails then give birth
to dozens of baby snails!

169
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:13,172
Good grief.

170
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:16,175
They have sex with anything
that comes their way?

171
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:21,347
I'm a bit jealous… I mean, that's creepy.

172
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:26,560
- Ermes!
- Got it.

173
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:27,520
Smack!

174
00:11:30,272 --> 00:11:31,941
Stone Ocean!

175
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:41,450
No User has two Stands.

176
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:45,037
Weather Forecast can only
control the weather.

177
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:47,039
But this is entirely different.

178
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:50,000
Just what is going on?

179
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:56,966
STAND NAME: WEATHER FORECAST
STAND MASTER: WEATHER FORECAST

180
00:11:58,008 --> 00:12:00,719
Back when life first began to emerge
in the form of plants,

181
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:04,515
oxygen began to form.

182
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:07,351
Oxygen is made up of O2,

183
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:11,105
which bonds with a third oxygen molecule.

184
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:13,774
Ozone consists of O3 molecules.

185
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:17,862
The ozonosphere occurs
at altitudes of 20 kilometers

186
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:20,865
to 25 kilometers.

187
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:25,786
If this ozone layer
were compromised in any way,

188
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:28,956
what would become of life on Earth?

189
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:33,711
Humans cannot predict
irregularities in weather patterns.

190
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:37,840
We can only analyze past weather patterns

191
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:40,009
collected over decades.

192
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:45,306
I'm going ahead!

193
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:47,933
Where is he? He has to be here.

194
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,810
He must be close by.

195
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:52,646
I'll find him and seize the disc,

196
00:12:53,481 --> 00:12:56,066
before it's handed to that foundation!

197
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:59,195
He'll probably head to the hospital

198
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:02,948
because he won't abandon Jolyne!

199
00:13:03,532 --> 00:13:06,744
The one who goes in to find Jolyne
must be Emporio!

200
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:09,788
He'll be the one who's going
opposite everyone else.

201
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:13,542
Dammit! I refuse to lose!

202
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:16,170
I'm going to live a happy life!

203
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:21,342
Jolyne, I wish I could help.

204
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:22,426
But…

205
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:26,305
I have to go deliver this disc
to the Foundation's messenger!

206
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:32,353
I promised Jolyne to get
her father's disc to the Foundation.

207
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:36,565
The Foundation rep said
to meet in five minutes!

208
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,109
Dammit!

209
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,612
What the hell?

210
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:44,406
No one is headed toward the hospital!

211
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:46,492
He has to be in the area.

212
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:48,953
I just know it!

213
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,175
Hello? Jolyne?

214
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:05,636
Hello?

215
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:17,690
I got you now.

216
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:21,944
Thanks, Netherworld.
The earth never fails me.

217
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:25,614
The memory of Jolyne had his number!

218
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:29,118
Emporio relayed the survivors'
seat numbers to Jolyne

219
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:31,287
using his cell phone!

220
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:36,250
Meaning, Jolyne knows his cell number!

221
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:39,837
Who would've thought
Emporio was a little boy?

222
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:45,092
Even the priest
didn't know about this kid.

223
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:53,350
What's this? He doesn't have the disc.

224
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:57,021
Moreover, he doesn't have his
phone either.

225
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:58,939
He had it a moment ago!

226
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,442
Hold on, I need to keep my head cool.

227
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:04,653
I can excavate to learn
what he did with the disc.

228
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,113
I can watch him put it away!

229
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,908
Oh, shit.

230
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:09,992
It's them!

231
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:20,961
- Are you sure he came this way, Jolyne?
- Yeah.

232
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:22,922
I feel his presence over here.

233
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:27,092
I'm sure I saw Emporio going this way.

234
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:30,387
Wait, do you think he's after Emporio?

235
00:15:30,471 --> 00:15:31,972
Impossible.

236
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:35,643
Even the priest doesn't know
about Emporio, so how can Versus know?

237
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:39,313
- That's…
- Emporio!

238
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,445
Watch out! Jump!

239
00:15:53,827 --> 00:15:55,329
Disgusting!

240
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,666
These are real, all right.

241
00:15:58,749 --> 00:15:59,792
Not illusions.

242
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:03,128
So slimy and gross.

243
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:12,888
Ermes!

244
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:20,479
Jolyne, go without me.

245
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:22,272
Go find Emporio!

246
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:25,275
That was definitely him getting dragged.

247
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:28,988
I don't know how he found out,
but Versus is after Emporio.

248
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:31,490
Stone Ocean!

249
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:37,079
Dammit.

250
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:38,288
My rope!

251
00:16:38,372 --> 00:16:40,791
My movements are slowed to snail's pace!

252
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,127
Emporio!

253
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:46,130
If you can hear me, pull on my rope!
Grab onto it!

254
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,174
Forty-five, sixty!

255
00:16:49,758 --> 00:16:50,926
Hut!

256
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:57,516
Jolyne!

257
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,019
This is Florida.

258
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:02,896
I dug up memories about the Superbowl.

259
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,481
Jolyne Cujoh,

260
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:08,110
the quarterback will carry you
all the way to the touchdown line.

261
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:09,361
My thread!

262
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:11,739
You are too slow to do anything.

263
00:17:11,822 --> 00:17:15,159
Bye. You're too far away now.

264
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:18,370
Yikes, I shouldn't touch these snails.

265
00:17:19,955 --> 00:17:21,415
I wasn't wrong.

266
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:25,544
He had Jotaro's disc just moments ago.

267
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:29,757
A second later,
his disc suddenly disappears.

268
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,259
He must have used his Stand ability.

269
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:36,764
He's able to stash things
with his ability.

270
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:39,975
Then where did he put the disc?

271
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,435
I should check again.

272
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:44,605
What?

273
00:17:45,522 --> 00:17:47,066
Where's Jolyne?

274
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:49,818
She's a snail. She can't move quickly!

275
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:04,208
Unbelievable, she caught up to him.

276
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:05,501
She rolled over!

277
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:08,796
She squeezed into a streetlight pole
that broke in half.

278
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:13,217
Now that her body has turned gooey,
she can easily fit in a metal pole!

279
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:17,387
Netherworld!

280
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:20,974
I didn't expect you to roll yourself over,

281
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:22,810
but this doesn't change a thing.

282
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:25,604
You are still powerless
against my Netherworld!

283
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:29,691
I excavated a certain memory.

284
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,736
Memory of ocean water
evaporating and leaving salt!

285
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:37,783
Snails and slugs can't stand salt!

286
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:42,955
What?

287
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,670
Shit, where is it?

288
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:53,006
I know you have the disc somewhere.

289
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:54,633
You've hidden it somewhere.

290
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:57,094
Where did you stash it?

291
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:07,020
I see, so our Stands work similarly.

292
00:19:07,104 --> 00:19:10,858
His Stand controls
the memories of objects.

293
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:13,193
I did it!

294
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,195
I found Jotaro's memory disc!

295
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:16,655
It's mine now!

296
00:19:16,738 --> 00:19:18,866
I win!

297
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:21,034
And now, finally,

298
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:24,037
I'm a step closer to the heaven
that priest is after!

299
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:25,998
Jolyne!

300
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,584
I'm sorry, Emporio.

301
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:31,378
I used you as bait.

302
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:33,964
You touched me,

303
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:37,259
and he touched you.

304
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:40,220
Feeling the sensation… All at once…

305
00:19:42,764 --> 00:19:45,601
I'm so slow!

306
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,991
Damn right, he's ours now!

307
00:20:01,074 --> 00:20:02,659
Nice going, Jolyne!

308
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,498
Emporio.

309
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:12,502
It's no use.

310
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:16,298
The Speedwagon Foundation's messenger
can't enter the city limits.

311
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:17,883
He's just standing by.

312
00:20:17,966 --> 00:20:19,134
Is that right?

313
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:23,805
Nicely done.

314
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,390
You got it, carjacker.

315
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:27,601
Let me set things straight.

316
00:20:27,684 --> 00:20:30,187
I've never stolen a car.

317
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:31,939
I'm messing with you.

318
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:33,982
You're coming with us.

319
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:37,277
Don't even think about running again.

320
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:39,446
I know.

321
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:44,952
What's this?

322
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:48,455
Are these the driver's shells?

323
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:51,166
But why just shells?

324
00:20:53,293 --> 00:20:54,628
Shells here too.

325
00:20:55,837 --> 00:20:59,466
Okay, I'm catching on.

326
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:07,933
I don't know what Weather did
to transform people into snails.

327
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:11,561
But I do know what lies ahead of us.

328
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:16,108
The snails' natural enemies
which feed on them.

329
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:19,778
Snails can only move slowly,

330
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:22,197
so they often die like this.

331
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:25,784
These beetles stick their heads
inside the shells

332
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:28,370
and devour the snails!

333
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:31,290
That's why these beetles are called
snail eaters!

334
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:33,875
These buggers!

335
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:41,425
Hey Weather!

336
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,552
I said wait up! Hey!

337
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:46,888
What's going on?

338
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:48,849
Did you cause this?

339
00:21:48,932 --> 00:21:52,352
Weather! What have you done?

340
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:56,606
Silence, Anastasia.

341
00:21:57,733 --> 00:22:00,652
He is closing in on us.

342
00:22:01,778 --> 00:22:04,448
He is within a 20-meter radius.

343
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,451
Him? You mean, Father Pucchi?

344
00:22:08,076 --> 00:22:09,036
He's here.

345
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:12,372
My sole purpose in life

346
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:14,708
is to settle my score with him.

347
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
